  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Showers will be more scattered nature into Friday, with best\nchance east of the Blue Ridge.\n\nA frontal boundary pushes slowly east today, reaching the\nPiedmont tonight. Low pressure will form along the Florida\nPanhandle this evening and lift northeast along the front late\ntonight. Models show better coverage of showers tonight into\nFriday morning east of the U.S. 29 corridor in VA into the NC\nPiedmont. As the wave moves by Friday morning will see drying\ntrend take shape. Another shortwave and front may bring some\nupslope showers Friday night-Sat morning in WV. Could even have\na few snowflakes in the higher ridges of Greenbrier County.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Unseasonably warm temperatures continue through \nFriday, returning to near normal this weekend. \n\nSouth winds ahead of the approaching front will maintain mild \nconditions with above normal temperatures today lingering into\nFriday. Once the front moves off the coast Friday, cold/dry \nadvection will set in for Friday night and continue through the \nweekend. This will promote temperatures returning to near\nnormal into next week.",
